WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.777
After leaving Patty's Place, Anne and Priscilla went straight to Phil's boardinghouse to tell her the good news.

2
00:00:07.778 --> 00:00:12.833
"Well, what has happened to you two? Why, you're actually shining!

3
00:00:12.834 --> 00:00:16.303
What's up?" Phil said when she answered the door.

4
00:00:16.304 --> 00:00:23.739
"Priscilla and I are going to live in Patty's Place next winter," said Anne triumphantly.

5
00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:31.004
"We've rented it," Priscilla continued, "and our friend Stella Maynard is coming, and she's moving in with us!"

6
00:00:31.005 --> 00:00:35.064
Suddenly Phil got down on her knees before Anne and Priscilla.

7
00:00:35.065 --> 00:00:39.111
"Oh, please let me come too! I'll be so good.

8
00:00:39.112 --> 00:00:47.173
If there's no room for me, I'll sleep in the little doghouse in the backyard! Please let me be your roommate!"

9
00:00:47.174 --> 00:00:56.469
"Get up, silly!" said Anne. She then said slowly, "Phil, we'd love that, but I'll be honest.

10
00:00:56.470 --> 00:01:01.283
I'm poor, Priscilla is poor, Stella Maynard is poor.

11
00:01:01.284 --> 00:01:04.788
The house and food will be simple and plain.

12
00:01:04.789 --> 00:01:11.183
You come from a wealthy family, and you live in an expensive boardinghouse, with fancy meals.

13
00:01:11.184 --> 00:01:16.862
Are you sure that you want a simple life, living with poor students?"

14
00:01:16.863 --> 00:01:21.062
"Oh, what do I care?" said Phil dramatically.

15
00:01:21.063 --> 00:01:26.951
"I'd live on bread and water—with just a little jam—if you'll let me move in."

16
00:01:26.952 --> 00:01:32.635
"Well, Phil, there would also be many chores to do," Anne continued.

17
00:01:32.636 --> 00:01:38.472
"At the moment you have a maid, but at Patty's Place, you would have to—"

18
00:01:38.473 --> 00:01:43.165
"I'll learn how to cook and clean!" Phil interrupted.

19
00:01:43.166 --> 00:01:46.794
"There's just one more thing," said Priscilla.

20
00:01:46.795 --> 00:01:52.692
"As all Redmond students know, Phil, you entertain visitors almost every evening.

21
00:01:52.693 --> 00:01:58.815
You have a very busy social life. Now at Patty's Place, we can't do that.

22
00:01:58.816 --> 00:02:04.830
We have decided we'll have visitors on Friday evenings only. How does that sound?"

23
00:02:04.831 --> 00:02:16.145
"Oh, that's fine," said Phil. "I knew I should have had a rule like that, but I couldn't decide on what day! You know how indecisive I am!"

24
00:02:16.146 --> 00:02:22.313
"Well," said Anne, "of course, we must check with Stella, but I'm sure she'll agree."

25
00:02:22.314 --> 00:02:31.049
"And if you get tired of our simple life, you can move out of Patty's Place, and no questions asked," added Priscilla.

26
00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:36.654
Phil hugged them both jubilantly, and Anne and Priscilla went home to the boardinghouse.

27
00:02:36.655 --> 00:02:40.922
"I hope things will be all right," said Priscilla soberly.

28
00:02:40.923 --> 00:02:45.005
"Phil's a great friend, but how will she be to live with?"

29
00:02:45.006 --> 00:02:49.196
"Who knows how any of us will get along?" Anne pointed out.

30
00:02:49.197 --> 00:02:56.516
"It's not as if Phil is selfish; she's just a little thoughtless. I think it will be fun!"

31
00:02:56.517 --> 00:03:00.742
At the end of the term, Anne won the English scholarship.

32
00:03:00.743 --> 00:03:05.900
She was overjoyed since she could now support herself and not rely on Marilla.

33
00:03:05.901 --> 00:03:09.215
Anne went back to Avonlea for the vacation.

34
00:03:09.216 --> 00:03:17.021
People told Anne she hadn't changed much, in a tone that hinted they were surprised and a little disappointed that she hadn't.

35
00:03:17.022 --> 00:03:23.658
Avonlea had not changed either. At least, so it seemed.

36
00:03:23.659 --> 00:03:28.128
But then Anne learned that Billy Andrews had married Nettie Blewett.

37
00:03:28.129 --> 00:03:31.055
She saw them together in church on Sunday.

38
00:03:31.056 --> 00:03:36.562
Anne's real surprise, though, was Ruby Gillis. What had happened to her?

39
00:03:36.563 --> 00:03:45.709
She was as beautiful as ever, but her blue eyes were too bright, her cheeks were too flushed, and she was very thin.

40
00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:55.735
"Is Ruby Gillis sick? She looks so different," Anne said to Mrs. Lynde as they walked home from church. Marilla frowned and looked sad.

41
00:03:55.736 --> 00:04:01.078
Mrs. Lynde said bluntly, "Ruby Gillis is dying of tuberculosis.

42
00:04:01.079 --> 00:04:06.343
Everybody knows it except Ruby and her family. They won't admit it.

43
00:04:06.344 --> 00:04:11.286
If you ask them about Ruby, they say she's perfectly healthy."

44
00:04:11.287 --> 00:04:19.281
Anne listened in shocked silence. Ruby Gillis, her old school friend, dying? Could it be possible?

45
00:04:19.282 --> 00:04:25.299
In recent years they had grown apart, and Ruby and Anne had not talked as much as they used to.

46
00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:31.263
But the old schoolgirl friendship was still there—fun, beautiful, silly Ruby!

47
00:04:31.264 --> 00:04:37.378
It was impossible to think of her and something as tragic as death in the same thought.

48
00:04:37.379 --> 00:04:42.032
Ruby had greeted Anne after church and urged her to come visit the next day.

49
00:04:42.033 --> 00:04:48.190
Anne had agreed, and so the next evening, Diana and Anne walked to the Gillis' house.

50
00:04:48.191 --> 00:04:54.443
"It's so awful to hear Ruby chatting and pretending nothing is wrong," Diana told Anne.

51
00:04:54.444 --> 00:04:59.534
"Sometimes she can hardly speak because she's coughing so much."

52
00:04:59.535 --> 00:05:05.571
Diana and Anne arrived at the Gillis' home, where many young male visitors had already arrived.

53
00:05:05.572 --> 00:05:14.303
Everyone was in the parlor, and two young men from Avonlea, Leonard Kimball and Alan Bell, were competing for Ruby's attention.

54
00:05:14.304 --> 00:05:18.579
Ruby was dressed in white, and her eyes and cheeks were bright.

55
00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:23.570
She giggled and chatted with her male admirers for most of the evening.

56
00:05:23.571 --> 00:05:29.924
At one point Ruby took Anne upstairs to her bedroom to show Anne some of her new summer clothes.

57
00:05:29.925 --> 00:05:34.212
"How do you like my new white hat? It's the latest fashion.

58
00:05:34.213 --> 00:05:37.152
I liked the hat you wore to church yesterday."

59
00:05:37.153 --> 00:05:40.980
She turned, holding the hat to her head with one hand.

60
00:05:40.981 --> 00:05:45.204
"Anne, did you see those two Avonlea boys downstairs?

61
00:05:45.205 --> 00:05:51.986
They're nice, but Tony Spencer is the one I really like. He couldn't come tonight."

62
00:05:51.987 --> 00:05:58.114
Ruby gave a shallow little laugh. Anne looked at the ground; she didn't know what to say.

63
00:05:58.115 --> 00:06:03.966
Just for a moment her eyes met Ruby's, and Anne saw something that made her heart ache.

64
00:06:03.967 --> 00:06:07.801
"Come and see me while you're home, please, Anne?" whispered Ruby.

65
00:06:07.802 --> 00:06:12.692
"I want to see you. I've missed having an old friend like you around . . ."

66
00:06:12.693 --> 00:06:16.685
"Are you feeling all right, Ruby?" Anne asked.

67
00:06:16.686 --> 00:06:21.369
"Me?" Ruby replied. "Why, I'm perfectly healthy, Anne.

68
00:06:21.370 --> 00:06:28.958
Of course, last winter I had the flu, and I had a slow recovery, but now I am all right. I don't look sick, surely?"

69
00:06:28.959 --> 00:06:33.460
Ruby's voice was almost bitter, as if Anne had accused her of something.

70
00:06:33.461 --> 00:06:44.863
Then Ruby went quickly downstairs and talked just to the young men, as if Anne and Diana were not there.

